{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Phase 1 RCA / debug dossier\n\nStep 0(a): searched `PowerShell ParserError setup-uv checksum asset expectedHash actualHash` and open/in_progress bugs; only this ticket matched.\nStep 0(b): report text names main commit 5ff99170b5d0cf97f2f639f117f4b9337622ba33 as the failing build floor. Suspect paths changed afterward in 024a6a2278134128be0c76c8d7c60e41b4ba817d (`Fix setup-uv PowerShell checksum parsing`).\nStep 0(c): investigation worktree is current at 952f0825321c755f41edce412ad1fe9f1db9268d = origin/main.\n\nProven root cause: `.github/actions/setup-uv/action.yml` as introduced by 5ff99170b5d0cf97f2f639f117f4b9337622ba33 contained `throw \"Checksum mismatch for $asset: expected $expectedHash, got $actualHash\"` in the embedded `pwsh` block (original action line 70). In a PowerShell double-quoted string, `$asset:` is parsed as a scoped/drive-qualified variable token rather than variable `$asset` followed by literal `:`, so the script fails during parsing before any install/test command can run. Legitimate scoped references such as `$env:RUNNER_OS`, `$env:RUNNER_ARCH`, `$env:GITHUB_PATH`, and `$env:GITHUB_OUTPUT` are not defects.\n\nProof: failing CI run 33574990286 at 5ff99170 shows Linux lint setup log `ParserError ... .ps1:51` pointing exactly at `$asset:` in the checksum-mismatch throw. The current action has `throw \"Checksum mismatch for ${asset}: expected $expectedHash, got $actualHash\"`; grep/static scan of `.github/actions/setup-uv/action.yml` finds no non-scope `$name:` hazards remaining. No local `pwsh` executable is installed, so OS execution proof comes from CI: Gerrit Verify run 33575422978 passed all setup-dependent jobs; main Test Suite (mirror) run 33578307020 reached `make lint`/`make typecheck` on Linux, pytest on macOS, and pytest on Windows after `Successfully installed uv 0.12.7` (Windows later failed in unrelated test collection, not action parsing). Later main Test Suite runs 33601203013 and 33632384491 are green.\n\nDefect origin: attributed to ticket 5caa-4b63-7ea2-4e71 via introducing commit 5ff99170b5d0cf97f2f639f117f4b9337622ba33, which added the repo-local setup-uv action and the offending checksum throw. I recorded the caused_by edge after attaching the introducing commit to 5caa because the MCP link gate did not see the commit reference; no force was used.\n\nPhase 2 plan/fix already landed in Gerrit change 2501: brace the asset interpolation as `${asset}:`, extend `scripts/check_uv_pin.py` with a portable static guard for non-scope `$name:` in the local action, and add regression coverage in `tests/unit/test_uv_pin_guard.py`. File impact recorded on this ticket for those three paths."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788370785747788914,"uuid":"ca5651f5-baf0-45ce-9d83-00a641b44fda"}